Why this licence
----------------

It is not a preference; it is the only choice that fits what the app already
contains. Vessel vendors the Winlator X server (LGPL-2.1) directly into the APK,
so the app's own terms have to be LGPL-compatible.

"or later" is the load-bearing part. libadrenotools is LGPL-3.0, and LGPL-2.1
*only* cannot be combined with it; the "or any later version" clause is what
permits that combination. Choosing bare LGPL-2.1 would quietly rule out a
component this project expects to link.

GPL-3.0 would also have been compatible and was rejected as stricter than the
obligation requires: it would impose full copyleft on the whole application
where the LGPL only asks that the LGPL parts stay free and relinkable.


What this means in practice
---------------------------

The obligation created by section 6 is that a user must be able to relink the
app against their own modified build of the LGPL parts. Two things satisfy it,
and both are already true:

  - The vendored source is in this public repository, unobfuscated and
    buildable, with its upstream commit recorded.
  - R8 does not rename or strip the com.winlator packages. Keep rules in
    app/proguard-rules.pro enforce that. If minification ever starts touching
    them, it is a licensing regression, not a build one.

Third-party components are not covered by this file. Each keeps its own licence
and its own copyright headers; see docs/LICENSING.md for the full picture,
including the components shipped as separate .wcp packages rather than compiled
into the app.
